    short: 'Unqualified assent to the terms of an offer; any change is a counter-offer.',
    extended: '<p><strong>Acceptance</strong> is the unqualified assent to all terms of the offer &mdash; the "mirror image" rule. Any change to terms is a <em>counter-offer</em>, which destroys the original offer and substitutes a new one capable of acceptance by the original offeror.</p><p>In commercial drafting, acceptance must be communicated; silence does not generally constitute acceptance (<em>Felthouse v Bindley</em> (1862) 11 CB(NS) 869).</p>',
