    short: 'The fourth element of contract formation in common law; presumed in commercial dealings.',
    extended: '<p>The fourth ingredient of contract formation under English and US (Delaware) law: parties must objectively intend their agreement to be legally binding. Presumed in commercial dealings; rebuttable by clear evidence (e.g. an "honour clause", a "subject to contract" header, or a comfort letter that disclaims binding effect).</p>',
