    extended: '<p><strong>Quality of Earnings (QoE)</strong> is the principal output of financial due diligence: an adjusted EBITDA bridge that strips out one-off, non-recurring, accounting-policy and revenue-recognition items to arrive at a "normalised" EBITDA used for valuation.</p><p>The QoE feeds directly into deal economics: the multiple is applied to the QoE-adjusted figure, not the reported figure. Working-capital and net-debt schedules typically accompany the QoE.</p>',
