    extended: '<p>See <em>Paramount-v-QVC</em>. <em>Paramount Communications, Inc. v QVC Network, Inc.</em>, 637 A.2d 34 (Del. 1994) clarified that <em>Revlon</em> enhanced scrutiny is triggered on a <strong>change-of-control transaction</strong> &mdash; defined as a transaction shifting voting control from a fluid public stockholder base to a single buyer or controller &mdash; rather than only when "sale is inevitable" (the original 1986 formulation).</p>',
